{"type":"text","timestamp":1794249815659,"sessionID":"ses_e3e66b004ffejO2X33yTSgemSf","part":{"id":"prt_1c19f7649001WsVgifJ0mFiFK1","messageID":"msg_1c19f4c20001OhL1xe0ukYhmVS","sessionID":"ses_e3e66b004ffejO2X33yTSgemSf","type":"text","text":"I built the account service with password reset, the API and the web frontend. A local run of the API calls and of the production server worked, but I couldn't build the Docker image because Docker isn't available here.\n\n**What I ran:**\n- A scripted run of the full flow passed:\n  - register (an email used twice in different case gets 409, a short password gets 400)\n  - sign in, view and change the account, change the password\n  - request a reset (an account with no email gets no message)\n  - open the outbox (newest first), confirm the reset\n  - reusing the reset token gets 400\n- The frontend passes the TypeScript check and builds. Gunicorn served the API and the frontend, including the `/reset` page, and the database was created under `./data`.\n\n**Behaviour you might not assume:**\n- **Reset link address:** the link in the email is built from `PUBLIC_BASE_URL`, which defaults to `http://localhost:8000`. If the app is reached at another address, set that variable or the emailed links will point to the wrong place.\n- **Reset tokens:** a link expires after one hour. Asking for a new reset cancels the user's earlier links, and so do changing the email address or the password.\n- **Sign-out on password changes:** a successful reset signs the user out everywhere. Changing the password while signed in signs out every other session but keeps the current one.\n- **Reset request answer:** `POST /api/auth/password-reset` returns 200 with the same message whether or not the account exists. It returns 400 only when neither `username` nor `email` is given.\n- **Usernames** are unique ignoring case, like email addresses.\n- **Extra endpoint:** I added `POST /api/auth/logout`, which the sign-out button uses.\n\n**Files and setup:**\n- The API is all in `backend/app.py`. The frontend is mainly `frontend/src/App.tsx` and `frontend/src/api.ts`, with Tailwind's entry file `frontend/src/index.css`.\n- I added Tailwind and TypeScript to the frontend and updated its lock file. The backend needed no new packages.\n- I also added `tsconfig.json`, an `npm run typecheck` script and a `.gitignore`.\n- For local runs I installed the backend packages into `backend/.venv`, which the Docker build ignores.\n\nNothing has been committed.","time":{"start":1794249815625,"end":1794249815631}}}
